      "start_seconds": 0.68,
      "end_seconds": 5.63,
      "duration_seconds": 4.95,
      "text": "Doctor? Hello, I hope this is the right time."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0002",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 7.23,
      "end_seconds": 11.31,
      "duration_seconds": 4.08,
      "text": "Yes, have a seat. Tell me what's going on."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0003",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 15.44,
      "end_seconds": 19.88,
      "duration_seconds": 4.44,
      "text": "Um, so... irregular periods. That's why I came."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0004",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 21.54,
      "end_seconds": 23.86,
      "duration_seconds": 2.32,
      "text": "Did it come on recently?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0005",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 28.98,
      "end_seconds": 38.95,
      "duration_seconds": 9.97,
      "text": "Probably two days. Yeah. I'd rather not end up on lots of tablets if I can avoid it."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0006",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 40.75,
      "end_seconds": 45.12,
      "duration_seconds": 4.37,
      "text": "Has there been extra hair on your chin too?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0007",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 48.65,
      "end_seconds": 51.11,
      "duration_seconds": 2.46,
      "text": "yeah. Two months, I'd say"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0008",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 52.59,
      "end_seconds": 58.28,
      "duration_seconds": 5.69,
      "text": "let me check a few things. Any milky nipple discharge or palpitations?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0009",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 60.3,
      "end_seconds": 63.83,
      "duration_seconds": 3.53,
      "text": "No, no milky nipple discharge or palpitations."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0010",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 64.37,
      "end_seconds": 67.44,
      "duration_seconds": 3.07,
      "text": "Hm, okay. Any sign of headaches?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0011",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 68.85,
      "end_seconds": 70.23,
      "duration_seconds": 1.38,
      "text": "Definitely no headaches."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0012",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 71.51,
      "end_seconds": 75.91,
      "duration_seconds": 4.4,
      "text": "Have you noticed any weakness, or anything odd with your balance?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0013",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 76.57,
      "end_seconds": 78.1,
      "duration_seconds": 1.53,
      "text": "Nothing odd there."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0014",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 80.07,
      "end_seconds": 85.39,
      "duration_seconds": 5.32,
      "text": "okay, any change in your bowel habit or your stomach generally?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0015",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 86.82,
      "end_seconds": 89.5,
      "duration_seconds": 2.68,
      "text": "no, that side's been fine"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0016",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 107.34,
      "end_seconds": 110.31,
      "duration_seconds": 2.97,
      "text": "has anyone ever diagnosed you with something?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0017",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 110.98,
      "end_seconds": 112.45,
      "duration_seconds": 1.47,
      "text": "I have diabetes."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0018",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 113.46,
      "end_seconds": 118.11,
      "duration_seconds": 4.65,
      "text": "Okay, I can see diabetes in your file as well."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0019",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 135.42,
      "end_seconds": 138.74,
      "duration_seconds": 3.32,
      "text": "Are you on your own at home?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0020",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 139.47,
      "end_seconds": 142.29,
      "duration_seconds": 2.82,
      "text": "I live with my elderly mother."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0021",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 142.95,
      "end_seconds": 145.8,
      "duration_seconds": 2.85,
      "text": "alright, do you get out much?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0022",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 146.4,
      "end_seconds": 150.17,
      "duration_seconds": 3.77,
      "text": "Not much, I mostly stay in these days."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0023",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 152.14,
      "end_seconds": 154.61,
      "duration_seconds": 2.47,
      "text": "Before we go further, any allergies?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0024",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 156.28,
      "end_seconds": 159.07,
      "duration_seconds": 2.79,
      "text": "I've never had an allergy."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0025",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 160.4,
      "end_seconds": 163.63,
      "duration_seconds": 3.23,
      "text": "Which medicines do you take at the moment?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0026",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 167.32,
      "end_seconds": 170.96,
      "duration_seconds": 3.64,
      "text": "Sitagliptin, 100 milligrams, once a day."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0027",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 172.67,
      "end_seconds": 176.17,
      "duration_seconds": 3.5,
      "text": "Let me get the readings out of the way."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0028",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 189.47,
      "end_seconds": 191.47,
      "duration_seconds": 2.0,
      "text": "Nearly done with the readings..."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0029",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 208.36,
      "end_seconds": 215.42,
      "duration_seconds": 7.06,
      "text": "okay: saturation 99 percent, temperature is 36.6 degrees, BP is 127 over 81, pulse 68."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0030",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 217.79,
      "end_seconds": 220.66,
      "duration_seconds": 2.87,
      "text": "Okay, time for me to examine you."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0031",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 236.8,
      "end_seconds": 238.61,
      "duration_seconds": 1.81,
      "text": "Yes, that's fine."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0032",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 239.58,
      "end_seconds": 241.79,
      "duration_seconds": 2.21,
      "text": "I'm just checking this side"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0033",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 258.94,
      "end_seconds": 268.8,
      "duration_seconds": 9.86,
      "text": "Your weight is up a little, and there is acne on the jaw and some coarse hairs on the chin."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0034",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 271.03,
      "end_seconds": 273.43,
      "duration_seconds": 2.4,
      "text": "You can sit up now."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0035",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 289.49,
      "end_seconds": 294.61,
      "duration_seconds": 5.12,
      "text": "Putting it all together, this looks most like polycystic ovary syndrome."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0036",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 296.44,
      "end_seconds": 298.38,
      "duration_seconds": 1.94,
      "text": "Is it dangerous, doctor?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0037",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 299.88,
      "end_seconds": 332.0,
      "duration_seconds": 32.12,
      "text": "I understand the worry at the moment I'd say it's polycystic ovary syndrome, and we'll know more once the a pelvic ultrasound is back i'll request a pelvic ultrasound, it'll help with irregular periods i'm going to order hormone blood tests, for irregular periods what I'm giving you is metformin, 500 milligrams, twice a day with food, long term that should help with polycystic ovaries it's a commonly used medicine and most people tolerate it well"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0038",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 333.91,
      "end_seconds": 344.07,
      "duration_seconds": 10.16,
      "text": "Regular exercise and a lower-sugar diet help the periods settle. Come back after the results. Does all of that that make sense?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0039",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 345.2,
      "end_seconds": 349.4,
      "duration_seconds": 4.2,
      "text": "Right, I'll do that. Thank you, doctor."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0040",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 350.02,
      "end_seconds": 351.21,
      "duration_seconds": 1.19,
      "text": "look after yourself"
    }
  ]
